# Issue #100 / #66 option (i): move the guard rule files under .claude/
#
# DRAFTED BY THE ASSISTANT, NOT APPLIED. Guard files (guard/, .claude/hooks/,
# .claude/settings*) are person-only under rule 5, so the owner applies this.
#
# Why the move: claude-code-action restores a fixed list of paths from a pull
# request's BASE branch, and `.claude` is on that list while a top-level
# `guard/` was not. With the rules outside `.claude/`, a `@claude` run on a
# pull request enforced THAT BRANCH's rules while running main's script.
# Moving the rules inside `.claude/` makes them come from the base branch too,
# with no new logic. Full explanation: docs/proposals/guard-into-claude.md.
#
# Generated against main at commit 926187c.
#
# Apply, from the repository root:
#
#     git apply docs/proposals/guard-into-claude.patch
#     node .claude/guard/selftest.mjs
